#: ../../source/recipes/glm5_3.rst:111
msgid ""
"**Single KV cache group.** Unlike the multi-group sparse-attention models"
" in this section, the validated ``zai-org/GLM-5.3`` checkpoint reports "
"one group (``group_tokens_per_block=[64]``). A ``-Flash`` variant of this"
" architecture additionally keeps a per-request kpool-tail scratch group "
"(``KpoolTailSpec``), which LMCache skips automatically; see "
":doc:`../mp/hybrid_models`. That variant is not covered by this "
"validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/glm5_3.rst:117
msgid ""
"Cached pages are byte-opaque views, so cache entries must not be shared "
"across engines with different attention backends or kernel block sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/glm5_3.rst:119
msgid ""
"The LMCache validation covers **text** generation with greedy decoding; "
"the cold and cache-served runs reproduced each other exactly."
msgstr ""

